/**
 * TERRA BELLUM — SEASON END (GDD §11, §12).
 *
 * The app shell routes here the instant `state.season.phase === 'ended'`, with
 * no top bar and no dock: this screen owns the whole viewport, so it also owns
 * the way onward.
 *
 * It is staged as a ceremony rather than a summary. Nine beats, every one of
 * them skippable with a tap, every one of them collapsing to its final state
 * under `prefers-reduced-motion`:
 *
 *   1 DARK     the frame drops, hairlines sweep, the season is named
 *   2 STAMP    the end-reason lands as a struck seal — annihilation, walkover
 *              or a points decision, each with genuinely different framing
 *   3 UNFURL   the winner's banner unrolls, their colour floods the frame
 *   4 NAME     the guild lands under a laurel with its motto and verdict
 *   5 PODIUM   the top three columns rise
 *   6 BOARD    the full leaderboard deals in, numbers counting up
 *   7 DOSSIER  the player's own record — their hexes, their split power, their
 *              harvest, their armies at the final bell
 *   8 AWARDS   superlatives derived from the real final state, including two
 *              that are not compliments
 *   9 OUTRO    the way onward
 *
 * Every number on screen comes out of the pure game modules — `guildStandings`
 * decides the order and the tiebreaker chain exactly as `evaluateSeason` did,
 * `powerOf` / `guildPower` own Power Points. Nothing is recomputed here.
 *
 * The world snapshot is FROZEN at the first ended state this screen sees: the
 * sandbox keeps simulating, and a scoreboard that drifts during its own medal
 * ceremony is not a scoreboard.
 */
